xxomdownxx@yahoo.com wrote:
> So, I'm only on dungeon level 3, and I find an armor shop.  And, much
> to my euphoria, I've found gauntlets of power, speed boots, and two
> cloaks:  a cloak of protection, and a cloak of displacement.  Question
> is, which should I be wearing?  I'm a level 4 priest, and without
> either my AC is 5.  Basically, which is going to keep me alive longer?

Probably protection, it's 3 extra points of AC and is one of the better
long-term cloaks (along with MR, oilskin, and protection).
Displacement is kind of nice for some foes but usually even a ranger
who starts with it wants to replace it pretty early on with one of the
MC3 cloaks, and protection's worth 3 extra AC right off the bat--people
go to huge lengths to get those extra AC points.

Displacement is just too unpredictable to really rely on, and there are
certain points in the game (mostly ranged weapon foes) where it's
actively bad for you, especially around drawbridges or with pets and
such; anything where confusing the opponents about your position could
be a big problem.  Plus, once you're invisible it's completely useless.
 Just not really worth it except in limited situations early on, IMO.



